<title>USA: Texas School Boards notes yield 3.95 pct in 1997.</title>
<headline>Texas School Boards notes yield 3.95 pct in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Southwest Co said Wednesday it tentatively priced $24.2 million Texas Association of School Boards one-year notes to yield 3.95 percent.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>TEXAS ASSOCIATION OF SCHOOL BOARDS</p>
<p>RE: $24,178,000*</p>
<p>TAX ANTICIPATION NOTES PROGRAM</p>
<p>CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION</p>
<p>SERIES 1996A</p>
<p>INTEREST WILL BE FIGURED ON A 30/360 BASIS (CODE 2).</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: MIG 1		 S&amp;P: NAF</p>
<p>FSA INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 09/05/1996	  FIRST COUPON:</p>
<p>DUE: 08/29</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>08/29/1997	     24,178M    4.75  %	  3.95</p>
<p>						  (Approx. $ Price 100.757)</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected Thursday, August 29, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on September 5, 1996.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry.</p>
<p>DTC is pending.</p>
<p>First Southwest Company</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
